{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And we went through all that great and terrible wilderness.</b> A way through which no man had passed, because of the multitude and size of the serpents and scorpions, as it says: נָחָשׁ שָׂרָף וְעַקְרָב (Deuteronomy 8:15). And the Sages of blessed memory already recounted that there were serpents like beams and scorpions like bows. And all this the blessed El did in order to shorten the way for them, so that they would enter the land immediately, before they would understand their figments of evil inclination and multiply in transgression. Yet all this did not suffice, for they sinned anyway — with the complainers, and with lust, and in the end with the spies."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase סִירוֹתֵיהֶם אֲטָד is difficult; rendered hyper-literally as 'their figments of evil inclination,' taking סירות in its rabbinic sense of base thoughts/imaginations. The construction with אֲטָד (thorn/bramble) may echo Numbers 33:55 or Judges 9:14-15; the exact reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:04.986002836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}